; claude: the game-making tools (CATALOG.md's section). Laid out like
; office/: the programs here, software/ for the golden frames, web/ for
; the browser.
;
; The tools making what any game can use: not one genre's levels,
; whose editor goes with the genre (TinySokobanEd, in games/puzzle/),
; nor what any program can use, a picture or a tune, whose tool goes in
; its medium's category (graphics/, music/). See games/README-tools.md
; for which goes where, and for how a game gets what a tool made: in
; the format of the playground layer that reads it, in a file the game
; embeds at build time.
;
; So far TinyAseprite, the sprite editor, and TinyTiled, the map
; editor: both over XPM files (one character per pixel, or per cell),
; read by Sprite and Tilemap.
; What it might contain next, each Tiny and after a famous original:
;  - a sound-effect maker (sfxr, Tomas Pettersson, 2007, for the Ludum
;    Dare game jams): sliders over audio/'s sfxr parameters, and a
;    button per kind of sound (a pickup, a laser, an explosion);
;  - a fantasy console's editors in one program (PICO-8, Joseph White,
;    2015): the sprites, map, sounds and music of one game.
(executables
  (names TinyAseprite TinyTiled)
  (modules TinyAseprite TinyTiled Mario_xpm)
  (libraries
    caps ; the authority to export files
    elm_playground
    elm_playground_native ; implem of virtual elm_playground
  )
)

; what the tools start from: TinyMario's hero (TinyAseprite) and its
; level (TinyTiled), the same files and the same rule as
; games/platform/dune's
(rule
 (targets Mario_xpm.ml)
 (deps
  (:stand %{project_root}/games/platform/mario_stand.xpm)
  (:walk1 %{project_root}/games/platform/mario_walk1.xpm)
  (:walk2 %{project_root}/games/platform/mario_walk2.xpm)
  (:jump %{project_root}/games/platform/mario_jump.xpm)
  (:level %{project_root}/games/platform/mario_level.xpm))
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   %{targets}
   (progn
    (echo "(* generated from games/platform/mario_*.xpm by apps/gamedev/dune *)\n")
    (echo "let stand = {|")
    (cat %{stand})
    (echo "|}\nlet walk1 = {|")
    (cat %{walk1})
    (echo "|}\nlet walk2 = {|")
    (cat %{walk2})
    (echo "|}\nlet jump = {|")
    (cat %{jump})
    (echo "|}\nlet level = {|")
    (cat %{level})
    (echo "|}\n")))))
